344 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/ActualText (New Zealand is located in the southwestern Pacific Ocean, approximately 1,200 miles \(1,900 kilometres\) southeast of Australia. It consists of two main land masses, the North Island and the South Island, as well as several smaller islands. )
/Pg 10 0 R
/K [3]
>>
endobj
345 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/ActualText (The country is situated in Oceania, the smallest continent in the world, also known as Australasia)
/Pg 10 0 R
/K [4]
>>
endobj
346 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/ActualText (Geography)
/Pg 10 0 R
/K [5]
>>
endobj
347 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/ActualText (New Zealand's geography is a captivating blend of natural wonders. From the towering peaks of the Southern Alps and the geothermal marvels of the North Island to the tranquil beauty of its lakes, beaches, and fiords, the country offers an astonishing array of landscapes. These diverse terrains have sculpted a playground for outdoor enthusiasts and a haven for those who appreciate nature's splendour. Whether you're drawn to the snow-capped mountains or the pristine coastlines, New Zealand's geography ensures that every corner of the country is a visual masterpiece waiting to be explored.)
/Pg 10 0 R
/K [6]
>>
endobj
348 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /Figure
/P 231 0 R
/Pg 10 0 R
/K [7]
>>
endobj
349 0 obj
<<
