/Type /StructElem
/S /H2
/T (. Alpine: The Southern Alps, which run through the South Island, have an alpine climate. This means colder temperatures year-round, with heavy snowfall in the winter, making it a popular destination for winter sports enthusiasts.)
/E (. Alpine: The Southern Alps, which run through the South Island, have an alpine climate. This means colder temperatures year-round, with heavy snowfall in the winter, making it a popular destination for winter sports enthusiasts.)
/Pg 12 0 R
/K [2]
>>
