393 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H2
/T (Politics and government New Zealand's government operates as a parliamentary democracy under a constitutional monarchy. It follows a system of government heavily influenced by the British model. The country's Head of State is the British monarch, represented by the Governor-General of New Zealand. The country's political culture emphasizes human rights, the rule of law, and a strong commitment to environmental sustainability, contributing to its reputation for stable and progressive governance.)
/E (Politics and government New Zealand's government operates as a parliamentary democracy under a constitutional monarchy. It follows a system of government heavily influenced by the British model. The country's Head of State is the British monarch, represented by the Governor-General of New Zealand. The country's political culture emphasizes human rights, the rule of law, and a strong commitment to environmental sustainability, contributing to its reputation for stable and progressive governance.)
