398 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 1070 0 R
/ActualText (Unique Biodiversity: New Zealand is home to a remarkable array of flora and fauna, much of which is found nowhere else in the world. This includes the kiwi bird, which is not only a national symbol but also a flightless and nocturnal bird native to New Zealand.)
/Pg 17 0 R
/K [2]
>>
endobj
399 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 1071 0 R
/ActualText (Maori Culture: The indigenous Maori people have a rich cultural heritage. The haka, a traditional Maori dance, is well-known worldwide, often performed by the national rugby team before matches.)
/Pg 17 0 R
/K [3]
>>
endobj
400 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 1072 0 R
/ActualText (Geothermal Wonders: The country sits on the Pacific Ring of Fire, resulting in geothermal activity. Rotorua, for example, is known for its geysers, hot springs, and bubbling mud pools. .)
/Pg 17 0 R
/K [4]
>>
endobj
