/S /P
/P 1073 0 R
/ActualText (Adventure Capital of the World: Queenstown is often referred to as the adventure capital of the world. It's a hub for various outdoor activities, including bungee jumping, skydiving, skiing, and water sports,)
/Pg 17 0 R
/K [5]
>>
endobj
402 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 1074 0 R
/ActualText (First Country to Grant Women the Right to Vote: New Zealand has a progressive history & and was the first self-governing country in the world to grant women the right to vote in 1893.)
/Pg 17 0 R
/K [6]
>>
endobj
403 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 1075 0 R
/ActualText (No Snakes: One interesting fact for those with ophidiophobia \(fear of snakes\) is that New Zealand is one of the few countries in the world where there are no native snake species. )
/Pg 17 0 R
/K [7]
>>
endobj
404 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 1076 0 R
/ActualText (Film Locations: The breathtaking landscapes of New Zealand have served as the backdrop for many famous movies, including the "Lord of the Rings" & "The Hobbit" trilogies directed by Peter Jackson. )
/Pg 17 0 R
/K [8]
>>
endobj
405 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 1077 0 R
/ActualText (Southern Hemisphere Stargazing: New Zealand, especially in the South Island, offers some of the best stargazing opportunities in the Southern Hemisphere. The Aoraki Mackenzie International Dark Sky Reserve is one of the best places to observe the night sky.)
/Pg 17 0 R
/K [9]
>>
endobj
406 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 1078 0 R
/ActualText (Longest Place Name: New Zealand is home to one of the longest place names in the world: Taumatawhakatangihangakoauauotamateaturipukakapikimaungahoronukupokaiwhenuakitanatahu. It is a hill in the Hawke's Bay region.)
/Pg 17 0 R
/K [10]
>>
endobj
407 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 1079 0 R
/ActualText (No Snails or Frogs: As well as having no native snake, New Zealand also lacks native land mammals \(except for bats\), & until human arrival, it had no land-based reptiles. It also doesn't have land snails or frogs)
/Pg 17 0 R
/K [11]
>>
endobj
