452 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/ActualText (Flying with kids can be a rewarding but challenging experience. Here are our top ten tips to help make your flight with kids more manageable and enjoyable:)
/Pg 21 0 R
/K [2]
>>
endobj
453 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/ActualText (1. Plan and Book in Advance:)
/Pg 21 0 R
/K [3]
>>
endobj
454 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/ActualText (Book your flights early to secure seating arrangements that work for your family. )
/Pg 21 0 R
/K [4]
>>
endobj
455 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/ActualText (Plan flights during times that align with your child's schedule, such as naptime or bedtime.)
/Pg 21 0 R
/K [5]
>>
endobj
456 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/ActualText (2. Prepare for Security Checkpoints:)
/Pg 21 0 R
/K [6]
>>
endobj
457 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/ActualText (Be organized and informed about the security screening process, including rules for carrying baby items and child supplies through security.)
/Pg 21 0 R
/K [7]
>>
endobj
458 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/ActualText (3. Pack Smart:)
/Pg 21 0 R
/K [8]
>>
endobj
459 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/ActualText (Pack a well-organized carry-on bag with essentials like diapers, wipes, a change of clothes, snacks, and entertainment items.)
/Pg 21 0 R
/K [9]
>>
endobj
460 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/ActualText (Consider using a backpack for easy access to items during the flight.)
/Pg 21 0 R
/K [10]
>>
endobj
461 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/ActualText (4 Entertainment and Distractions:)
/Pg 21 0 R
/K [11]
>>
endobj
462 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/ActualText (Bring a variety of entertainment, such as books, colouring books, toys, and electronic devices.)
/Pg 21 0 R
/K [12]
>>
endobj
463 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/ActualText (Download kid-friendly apps, movies, or games on tablets or smartphones.)
/Pg 21 0 R
/K [13]
>>
endobj
464 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/ActualText (5. Child-Friendly Seating:)
/Pg 21 0 R
/K [14]
>>
endobj
465 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/ActualText (Choose seating that works best for your family, such as bulkhead seats or a row with an empty middle seat.)
/Pg 21 0 R
/K [15]
>>
endobj
466 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/ActualText (Consider using child restraint devices, like CARES harnesses or approved car seats.)
/Pg 21 0 R
/K [16]
>>
endobj
