484 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/ActualText <FEFF00520065006C006F0063006100740069006E0067002000700065007400730020200B>
/Pg 23 0 R
/K [1]
>>
endobj
485 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/ActualText (We understand that for many, pets are an important part of the family, and will join you on your journey to Aotoroa, New Zealand. )
/Pg 23 0 R
/K [2]
>>
endobj
486 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/ActualText (We recommend starting the process well in advance, as the timeline for compliance with regulations can be quite lengthy. Engaging with a professional pet relocation service or consulting with the MPI in New Zealand can help ensure a smooth and successful transition for your pets to their new home.)
/Pg 23 0 R
/K [3]
>>
endobj
487 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /Figure
/P 244 0 R
/Pg 23 0 R
/K [0]
>>
endobj
488 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/ActualText (Here are some key steps to consider when relocating pets to New Zealand:)
/Pg 23 0 R
/K [4]
>>
endobj
489 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 1089 0 R
/ActualText (Check Eligibility: Ensure your pet is eligible for importation into New Zealand. Certain dog breeds, such as American Pit Bull Terriers, Brazilian Fila, and Dogo Argentino, are prohibited.)
/Pg 23 0 R
/K [5]
>>
endobj
490 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 1090 0 R
/ActualText (Microchipping: All cats and dogs must be microchipped for identification purposes. Make sure the microchip meets ISO standards.)
/Pg 23 0 R
/K [6]
>>
endobj
491 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 1091 0 R
/ActualText (Rabies Vaccination: Ensure your pet has up-to-date rabies vaccinations. These should be administered at least six months before travelling to New Zealand.)
/Pg 23 0 R
/K [7]
>>
endobj
492 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 1092 0 R
/ActualText (Blood Tests: Cats and dogs must have a rabies serology test to confirm that the vaccination is effective. This should be done at an approved laboratory.)
/Pg 23 0 R
/K [8]
>>
endobj
493 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 1093 0 R
/ActualText (Internal and External Parasite Treatment: Treat your pet for internal and external parasites, including tapeworms and ticks. These treatments should be administered within a specified timeframe before travelling.)
/Pg 23 0 R
/K [9]
>>
endobj
494 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H1
/T (p14)
/E (p14)
/Pg 23 0 R
/K [10]
>>
endobj
495 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 1094 0 R
/ActualText (Import Permit: Apply for an import permit from the Ministry for Primary Industries \(MPI\) in New Zealand. This is usually done several weeks before travel.)
/Pg 24 0 R
/K [0]
>>
endobj
496 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 1095 0 R
/ActualText (Quarantine: Pets must undergo a minimum of ten days of quarantine upon arrival in New Zealand. The quarantine facility should be pre-arranged and booked well in advance. There are four quarantine facilities in New Zealand.  More information on each facility can be found by clicking the following link: https://www.mpi.govt.nz/bring-send-to-nz/pets-travelling-to-nz/bringing-cats-and-dogs-to-nz/quarantine-facilities-and-importing-cats-and-dogs/)
/Pg 24 0 R
/K [1]
>>
endobj
497 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 1096 0 R
/ActualText (Transportation: Choose a reputable pet transport company with experience in relocating animals to New Zealand. They will help with flight arrangements, proper documentation, and meeting biosecurity requirements.)
/Pg 24 0 R
/K [2]
>>
endobj
498 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 1097 0 R
/ActualText (Health Certificates: Obtain an official veterinary health certificate for your pet issued shortly before departure. This certificate should confirm the pet's health and compliance with New Zealand's import regulations.)
/Pg 24 0 R
/K [3]
>>
endobj
499 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 1098 0 R
/ActualText (Pet Food and Toys: Ensure you follow New Zealand's regulations regarding bringing in pet food and toys, as some items may be subject to inspection and treatment.)
/Pg 24 0 R
/K [4]
>>
endobj
500 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 1099 0 R
/ActualText (Costs: Relocating pets to New Zealand can be expensive due to transportation, quarantine, and various health and compliance requirements. Be prepared for these costs.)
/Pg 24 0 R
/K [5]
>>
endobj
501 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 1100 0 R
/ActualText (Cats and Dogs Act: Familiarize yourself with New Zealand's Cats and Dogs Act, which imposes certain responsibilities on pet owners in New Zealand.)
/Pg 24 0 R
/K [6]
>>
endobj
