672 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/ActualText (New Zealand School Term Dates)
/Pg 38 0 R
/K [0]
>>
endobj
673 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/ActualText (In New Zealand, the school year is divided into four terms. The exact dates for each term can vary slightly from year to year, but generally, they follow a similar pattern)
/Pg 38 0 R
/K [1]
>>
endobj
674 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/ActualText (Term 1)
/Pg 38 0 R
/K [2]
>>
endobj
675 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/ActualText (Typically starts in late January or early February and runs until mid-April.)
/Pg 38 0 R
/K [3]
>>
endobj
676 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/ActualText (This term includes a break for Easter, which can fall in late March or early April.)
/Pg 38 0 R
/K [4]
>>
endobj
677 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/ActualText (Term 2:)
/Pg 38 0 R
/K [5]
>>
endobj
678 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/ActualText (Usually begins in late April or early May and continues until early July.)
/Pg 38 0 R
/K [6]
>>
endobj
679 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/ActualText (There is typically a two-week break in late May or early June, known as the mid-term break or school holidays.)
/Pg 38 0 R
/K [7]
>>
endobj
680 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/ActualText (Term 3:)
/Pg 38 0 R
/K [8]
>>
endobj
681 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/ActualText (Starts in mid-July and runs until late September or early October.)
/Pg 38 0 R
/K [9]
>>
endobj
682 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/ActualText (There may be a one-week break in mid-August, depending on the school's schedule.)
/Pg 38 0 R
/K [10]
>>
endobj
683 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/ActualText (Term 4:)
/Pg 38 0 R
/K [11]
>>
endobj
684 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/ActualText (Begins in mid-October and continues until mid-December.)
/Pg 38 0 R
/K [12]
>>
endobj
685 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/ActualText (This term includes a six-week summer break, starting in mid-December and ending in late January or early February, marking the end of one school year and the start of the next.)
/Pg 38 0 R
/K [13]
>>
endobj
686 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/ActualText (It's important to note that these dates are a general guide, and schools may have variations in their term dates or additional holiday periods, such as teacher-only days or local holidays. )
/Pg 38 0 R
/K [14]
>>
endobj
